<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 26 — WebSockets & Server-Sent Events: live order tracking.
    experiment/  short polling vs long polling vs SSE vs WebSocket over real sockets (bytes counted
                 by a proxy, a minimal RFC 6455 server checked by the JDK WebSocket client); how many
                 SSE streams a server holds on a 200-thread pool vs virtual threads; reconnect storms
    tracking/    Spring: SSE stream for customers (SseEmitter, Last-Event-ID replay, jittered retry,
                 heartbeats, load shedding) and a WebSocket endpoint for riders (handshake auth,
                 validation, rate limiting, ConcurrentWebSocketSessionDecorator)
-->
